      "content": "6. Impact of Economic Reforms"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "202ambd",
      "content": "• Increase in economic growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "plpzb3l",
      "content": "• Growth of private sector."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "71is35t",
      "content": "• Expansion of foreign investment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n06r7sd",
      "content": "• Improvement in technology and productivity."
    },
    {
      "id": "6xh8lgb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Challenges of Economic Reforms"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uuv48mj",
      "content": "• Increase in income inequality."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rlynjff",
      "content": "• Regional disparities."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The 1991 reforms are famously known as the Rao-Manmohan Model of Economic Development.",
        "A critical trigger for reforms was India's foreign exchange reserves dropping to less than two weeks' worth of imports in 1991.",
        "Abolition of industrial licensing for most projects was a key step under Liberalization."
      ],
      "id": "ezt7glh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hea1bt6",
      "content": "• Impact on small industries."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h0z25n6",
      "content": "• Employment challenges."
    },
    {
      "id": "72so2xe",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC / SSC Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gtn0xew",
      "content": "• Economic reforms in India started in 1991."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7w8rs9s",
      "content": "• The reforms are based on LPG policy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "khaqpbs",
      "content": "• LPG stands for Liberalization, Privatization and Globalization."
    }
